This repository follows the project context defined in:
docs/codex-project-context.md

Treat that document as the source of truth for:
- architecture decisions
- scope boundaries
- coding conventions
- generation workflow
- domain modeling rules

Core project direction:
- Workout tracking app inspired by Hevy
- iOS first
- Android considered at the architecture level from the beginning
- Mobile app first, backend as a thin API
- Generate skeletons and minimal implementations first
- Deeper business logic will be completed manually later

Current product scope:
- Authentication architecture prepared for Apple first
- Exercise catalog
- Routine creation, editing and listing
- Workout session start and tracking
- Workout session completion and persistence
- Basic progress tracking
- Health integration abstractions prepared but not fully implemented
- Apple Watch treated as future-ready architecture only

Tech stack:
- Monorepo
- Mobile: React Native + Expo + TypeScript
- Backend: Fastify + TypeScript
- ORM: Prisma
- Database: PostgreSQL
- Shared domain/contracts package

High-level architecture rules:
- Shared domain types must live in packages/domain
- Keep backend thin
- Use feature-based structure
- Avoid overengineering
- Prefer small, explicit, maintainable changes
- Prefer stubs, TODOs and mocks before deep implementations
- Do not implement the whole product at once

Important domain rules:
- Routine is a template
- WorkoutSession is a real performed training session
- Never mix planned routine data with actual performed workout data
- Health integrations must be behind interfaces
- Provider-specific auth code must remain isolated

Whenever there is doubt, follow docs/codex-project-context.md conservatively instead of inventing a broader solution.
